.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt RSA_PRIVATE_ENCRYPT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm RSA_private_encrypt ,
.Nm RSA_public_decrypt
.Nd low-level signature operations
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/rsa.h
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft int
.Fo RSA_private_encrypt
.Fa "int flen"
.Fa "unsigned char *from"
.Fa "unsigned char *to"
.Fa "RSA *rsa"
.Fa "int padding"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo RSA_public_decrypt
.Fa "int flen"
.Fa "unsigned char *from"
.Fa "unsigned char *to"
.Fa "RSA *rsa"
.Fa "int padding"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Both of the functions described on this page are deprecated.
Applications should instead use
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign_init_ex 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify_recover_init 3 ,
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify_recover 3 .
.Pp
These functions handle RSA signatures at a low-level.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_private_encrypt
signs the
.Fa flen
bytes at
.Fa from
(usually a message digest with an algorithm identifier) using the
private key
.Fa rsa
and stores the signature in
.Fa to .
.Fa to
must point to
.Sy RSA_size(rsa)
bytes of memory.
.Pp
.Fa padding
denotes one of the following modes:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It RSA_PKCS1_PADDING
PKCS #1 v1.5 padding.
This function does not handle the
.Sy algorithmIdentifier
specified in PKCS #1. When generating or verifying PKCS #1 signatures,
.Xr RSA_sign 3
and
.Xr RSA_verify 3
should be used.
.It RSA_NO_PADDING
Raw RSA signature.
This mode should
.Em only
be used to implement cryptographically sound padding modes in the
application code.
Signing user data directly with RSA is insecure.
.El
.Pp
.Fn RSA_public_decrypt
recovers the message digest from the
.Fa flen
bytes long signature at
.Fa from
using the signer's public key
.Fa rsa .
.Fa to
must point to a memory section large enough to hold the message digest
(which is smaller than
.Sy RSA_size(rsa) - 11 Ns ).
.Fa padding
is the padding mode that was used to sign the data.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn RSA_private_encrypt
returns the size of the signature (i.e., RSA_size(rsa)).
.Fn RSA_public_decrypt
returns the size of the recovered message digest.
.Pp
On error, -1 is returned; the error codes can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr RSA_sign 3 ,
.Xr RSA_verify 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify_recover 3
.Sh HISTORY
Both of these functions were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
